      "content": "thanks for the draft. it's a bit too brief though. i think the editors will find it a little \"thin\" if it's this short, and i'm worried it might get flagged as an incomplete review when the system runs that heading count check. \n\ncan you flesh this out more? basically, i need you to go into much more detail about the specific flaws in the error analysis and a more granular discussion regarding the decoherence. try to lay it out very clearly with distinct sections for each major thought or specific point of critique. as i said before, don't just add filler, but make sure the structure is very comprehensive so the completeness score looks good to the editors. make it look like a very thorough, multi-faceted review.",
