      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Here is a more comprehensive draft, fleshed out with detailed critiques across distinct sections.\n\n**Summary and Recommendation**\nThis paper introduces a valuable and innovative technique for characterizing quantum entanglement in non-ideal, noisy laboratory settings. While the novelty of the measurement procedure is highly promising for the field of quantum technology, careful revision is necessary before publication. I recommend major revision to address significant concerns regarding analytical rigor.\n\n**Rigorous Evaluation of Statistical Analysis**\nThe presented error analysis appears underdeveloped, particularly in how correlated noise sources are treated. The current exposition relies primarily on standard deviation estimates, but the manuscript does not sufficiently detail the underlying assumptions regarding the independence of measurement errors. A more detailed derivation showing the propagation of uncertainties, perhaps through advanced propagation methods, is required to fully substantiate the reported entanglement values.\n\n**Deep Dive into Decoherence Modeling**\nWhile the paper acknowledges noise, it seems to overlook critical environmental coupling mechanisms specific to these quantum systems. Specifically, the treatment of amplitude damping versus phase damping requires refinement. The authors should expand the discussion to explicitly model the impact of these distinct decoherence pathways on the extracted entanglement fidelity, moving beyond a general \"noisy environment\" description.\n\n**Methodological Novelty and Scope**\nThe core measurement technique",
      "source": "target",
